WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.070
The central and eastern tropical Pacific.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.910
Some years, its surface water
turns warmer than usual.

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:08.870
This is El Niño.

4
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.290
Episodes typically last nine to 12 months.

5
00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:15.830
Southern Africa, 2023 to 24.

6
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:21.530
The regional body SADC named El Niño the
primary driver of a significant increase

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.490
in food insecurity.

8
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.190
Did Pacific storms sink grain ships?

9
00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.430
How can warm water in the Pacific leave
families in southern Africa short of food?

10
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.230
In this mission, you'll
trace how shocks hit food,

11
00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:37.490
from wildfire and floods to drought.

12
00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.570
Then you'll follow an earthquake in Nepal,

13
00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.110
in 2015, from stored
grain to damaged roads.

14
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:48.850
Your mission: explain how warm water in
the Pacific can leave families in southern

15
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:50.680
Africa short of food.
